    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0291" n="195" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg195"/>

                <head>No. 145.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Schlözer.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 28th ultimo, inclosing a copy of a dispatch addressed to you
                    by the chancellor of the German Empire, from which it appears that no measures
                    have been taken by that government to obstruct emigration to the United States,
                    and that the statement published to that effect in the press of the country in
                    June last is without foundation.</p>
                <p>In compliance with your request I have caused the substance of the chancellor’s
                    note to be promulgated through the public press.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
